<p>As vice-president of the State Fair Association and prominent horse rancher from Flasher, Stephen P. Weekes was instrumental in the event’s development, along with his sons, Steve and Charlie. Weeke's son-in-law, Max Theil, created the "Heart River Roundup" in about 1918 and “Badlands Bill” McCarty joined the association and promoted the moniker "Mandan Roundup" starting in 1923.</p>
